Subject: [PATCH] =?UTF-8?q?P36:=20pgm=5Fbase=20=E2=80=94=20skip=20FindPyth?=
 =?UTF-8?q?onInterpreter=20in=20headless=20(kicad-cli)=20mode?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

PGM_BASE::InitPgm always tried to find a Python interpreter when the
user hadn't cached one, calling PYTHON_MANAGER::FindPythonInterpreter
which does up to three synchronous wxExecute() fork/exec calls
('which -a python3', 'which -a python'). ~10-30 ms wasted per startup.

kicad-cli almost never uses the Python API plugin runner. Guard on
!aHeadless. GUI users are unaffected.
---
 common/pgm_base.cpp | 10 ++++++++--
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/common/pgm_base.cpp b/common/pgm_base.cpp
index 531b47d2..da390ff2 100644
--- a/common/pgm_base.cpp
+++ b/common/pgm_base.cpp
@@ -470,8 +470,14 @@ bool PGM_BASE::InitPgm( bool aHeadless, bool aIsUnitTest )
     // Load common settings from disk after setting up env vars
     GetSettingsManager().Load( commonSettings );
 
-    // If user doesn't have a saved Python interpreter, try (potentially again) to find one
-    if( commonSettings->m_Api.python_interpreter.IsEmpty() )
+    // If user doesn't have a saved Python interpreter, try (potentially
+    // again) to find one — but only in GUI mode. FindPythonInterpreter
+    // does up to three synchronous `wxExecute(which -a python3)` fork/exec
+    // calls, which costs 10-30 ms on every startup for a feature (API
+    // plugin runner) that kicad-cli almost never uses. If a CLI user
+    // does want plugins, the GUI will find the interpreter on their
+    // first GUI launch and cache it into common settings.
+    if( !aHeadless && commonSettings->m_Api.python_interpreter.IsEmpty() )
         commonSettings->m_Api.python_interpreter = PYTHON_MANAGER::FindPythonInterpreter();
 
     // Init user language *before* calling loadSettings, because
